<newsitem itemid="137921" id="root" date="1996-10-23" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Ethical moves into red on increased R&amp;D.</title>
<headline>Ethical moves into red on increased R&amp;D.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended August 31</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		69.0 loss	    vs 17.0 profit</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 nil		    vs nil</p>
<p> Pretax		     11.0 loss	    vs 3.4 profit</p>
<p> Revenues		   13.8		   vs 18.8</p>
<p>NOTE - UK-based drug delivery research company Ethical Holdings Plc, which is listed on the U.S. Nasdaq exchange, said a 32 percent rise in research and development and the repurchase of product rights for 7.9 million stg helepd to push it into the red.</p>
<p> Operating result	 11.9 loss	    vs 3.1 profit</p>
<p> Exceptional		7.9 loss	     vs 0.8 loss</p>
<p> Interest receivable    1.0		    vs 0.5</p>
<p> Tax			  0.7 credit	   vs 1.2</p>
<p> Net taxed		  10.3 loss	    vs 2.3 profit</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
